  "description": "MAGFOR crystallizes in the monoclinic crystal system with space group C 2/c. Reported CIF formula moiety: C48 H44 N8 O4 S4 Yb4,2(C6 H14),4(C4 H8 O1). From the CIF bond table, Yb1 (Yb) has 3 O neighbors; Yb2 (Yb) has 3 O neighbors; Yb1A (Yb) has 3 O neighbors; Yb2A (Yb) has 3 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 6 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.577-3.904 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 99.10-114.21°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C48H44N8O4S4Yb4. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 1 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)).",
